Sample Bicep Deployment Commands:

1 Create full set of AI Agent resources with new dependent resources (Storage, CosmosDB, Search account)
az deployment group create --name ExampleDeployment --resource-group {ResourceGroup Name} --template-file {template path} --parameters newOrExisting=new foundryAccountName={new foundry account name}

2 Create full set of AI Agent resources with existing dependent resources (Storage, CosmosDB, Search account)

az deployment group create --name ExampleDeployment --resource-group {ResourceGroup Name} --template-file {template path} --parameters newOrExisting=existing cosmosDBAccountName={BYO CosmosDB account name} storageAccountName={BYO storage account name} aiSearchName={BYO search account name} foundryAccountName={new foundry account name}

*Current limitation
DocumentDB SQL role assignment will fail in bicep deployment due to new principle id replication delay on SQL service side.
Please grant the MI proper permission with following command: 
az cosmosdb sql role assignment create --subscription {sub id} --resource-group {rg name} --account-name {cosmosdb account name} --role-definition-name "Cosmos DB Built-in Data Contributor" --principal-id {project managed identity principle id} --scope "/"

and then run only the project caphost creation (it has been commented out in the main.bicep)